# @epistemologic/property/docblock_grounded — first of the trio of
# #53 property/fracture bilateral instances at doc-claim altitude.
# Sixth #53 family overall; landed per Seam Phase D ratification
# chain (`820a451` TICK 1 `shards/docblock.mirror` family-root RATIFY,
# `3283de4` TICK 2 `shards/epistemologic/liquid_extraction.mirror`
# sibling family-root RATIFY). Interpretation B canonical: narrative
# ABOVE `---`; `in` clauses + typed declarations BELOW, per Seam
# pre-review `docs/audits/2026-07-06-seam-arc-4-sub-arc-a-pre-review.md`
# §1.
#
# This shard is the DECLARATIVE HALF of the docblock grounding audit.
# The OPERATIONAL HALF lands at TICK 4 as
# `@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_ungrounded` per Mara spec
# `docs/specs/doc-code-seam-shards.md` §4 (routes via
# `@kintsugi/surface`'s `ashby_mismatch` class per compiler-error-
# surface §3.1). Bilateral discipline per recognition #53: the
# property side names WHAT grounds a docblock; the fracture side
# names WHAT TO DO when a docblock is ungrounded. The two land
# together in a paired atomic bundle at doc-claim altitude.
#
# === Sixth #53 family; first-of-trio at doc-claim altitude ===
#
# Recognition #53 (`[[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]`)
# names a substrate pattern: declarative property at
# `@epistemologic/property/<predicate>` + operational fracture body at
# `@kintsugi/fracture/<predicate>`, bridged by the kintsugi loop.
# Five prior instances landed:
#
# 1. `@kintsugi/fracture/keyword` (2026-06-10 `d908798`) — first.
# 2. `@mirror/fracture/predicate` (task #272 forward-promised) — second.
# 3. `dark_count_monotone` (2026-06-19 `499ffd9`) — third.
# 4. `cold_compile_within_tolerance` (2026-06-19) — fourth.
# 5. `@kintsugi/surface` + `ashby_variety_match` (2026-07-03 `e910dd6`)
#    — fifth.
#
# THIS SHARD is the sixth family's FIRST-OF-TRIO. The three properties
# in the trio (per Mara spec §3/§5/§7) are:
#
# - `docblock_grounded` — THIS SHARD. Every extractable claim in
#   a docblock is either a motivating claim, a forward-promise, or
#   has a citation whose ancestor exists on main with cited-content
#   matching the claim text.
# - `docblock_coherent` (TICK 5) — no two extracted predicates
#   contradict; no extracted predicate contradicts a below-seam
#   declaration.
# - `docblock_no_extraction_pattern` (TICK 7) — no unmarked
#   superlatives; hedged claims marked defer; citations content
#   match; claim size matches landing size.
#
# The trio decomposes docblock well-audited-ness into three
# independently-checkable predicates; each has a bilateral fracture
# body that routes ungrounded/incoherent/extractive docblocks
# through `@kintsugi/surface`. This shard is INDEPENDENT of the
# other two (only imports `@epistemologic/liquid_extraction` for
# `extractor_input`/`predicate_shape`, does not depend on
# coherence or extraction-pattern checks).
#
# === Predicate substance per Mara spec §3 ===
#
# The docblock-grounded predicate answers: is every claim this
# docblock makes either a motivating claim, a forward-promise, or
# grounded in an existing substrate ancestor whose content matches
# the claim text? In substrate narrative:
#
#   docblock_grounded(d) ⇔
#     ∀ claim ∈ extract_claims(d):
#       claim.kind ∈ {motivating_claim, forward_promise} ∨
#       (claim.citation ≠ empty_ref ∧
#        ancestor_exists_on_main(claim.citation) ∧
#        cited_content_matches_claim(claim.citation, claim.text))
#
# Three sub-obligations per claim:
#
# - `extract_claims(d)` is @docblock's routing action (declared at
#   TICK 1's `shards/docblock.mirror`) that walks the docblock's
#   `#`-narrative and lifts each substantive assertion to a
#   `doc_claim` with `kind`, `citation`, and `text` fields per
#   the @docblock carrier surface.
#
# - Kind-check exemption: `motivating_claim` and `forward_promise`
#   are the two kinds the substrate honors as ungrounded-by-design.
#   Motivating claims name the "why" (no citation obligation).
#   Forward-promises name commitments the substrate will honor at
#   named future ticks (obligation deferred, not waived). Both
#   route past the citation check.
#
# - Citation-check body: for `grounded_claim` and `candidate_claim`
#   kinds, the citation must be non-empty (`empty_ref` is the
#   substrate's null-citation carrier), the citation must resolve
#   to an ancestor on main (not a dangling reference; not a branch-
#   local commit), and the cited content must match the claim text
#   (content-addressed check per the substrate's OID discipline —
#   the citation IS the ancestor's OID; the match verifies the
#   ancestor's content bytes ground the claim's assertion).
#
# The extractor body (`extract_predicate` in
# `@epistemologic/liquid_extraction`) is forward-promised per TICK
# 2's landing per `[[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]`; until it lands,
# `docblock_grounded`'s body discharges at splinter(ast) altitude
# with the extractor's output shape. `ancestor_exists_on_main` and
# `cited_content_matches_claim` are sibling predicates the property
# body composes against; they compose from the substrate's landed
# content-addressing discipline (OID resolution + byte-match).
#
# === Sibling coupling to @docblock + @epistemologic/liquid_extraction ===
#
# This shard's `in @docblock` grounds the sibling-coupling to TICK
# 1's family-root: the `doc_claim` carrier lifted through the
# property predicate here is exactly @docblock's `doc_claim`. The
# `in @epistemologic/liquid_extraction` grounds the sibling-coupling
# to TICK 2's family-root: the extractor's output shape
# (`predicate_shape` splinter(ast) fragment) is the surface this
# property's body discharges over. Both sibling family-roots are
# COUPLED via this shard: the property answers a question the
# substrate can only ask at the intersection of the doc-claim
# carrier and the liquid-extraction surface.
#
# === Path-namespace property ===
#
# This file at
# `shards/epistemologic/property/docblock_grounded.mirror` declares
# `@epistemologic/property/docblock_grounded` at species-depth 2
# under @epistemologic per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.
# The depth mirrors the four landed siblings at
# `@epistemologic/property/{cold_compile_within_tolerance,
# dark_count_monotone, restart_intensity_well_formed}`: this
# shard sits in the same species column and is subject to the
# same path-namespace pact.
#
# === Circular-reflexive self-audit ===
#
# Per Mara's projection-surface spec `63bdecc` §6 the operator
# must audit its own audit at depth=3. This shard's own docblock
# is subject to `docblock_grounded(this_docblock)` at logical
# altitude. Substrate-honest verdict at THIS shard's state:
#
# The narrative above makes seven citations — five to prior #53
# instance commits (`d908798`, `499ffd9`, `e910dd6`, `499ffd9`,
# task #272 forward-promise), two to Seam ratification commits
# (`820a451`, `3283de4`), and multiple to substrate documents
# (Mara spec §3, projection-surface §6, doc-code-seam pre-review
# §1). Of those:
#
# - Ratification commits `820a451`, `3283de4` — `grounded_claim`
#   kind, citation is the OID, ancestor exists on main by the
#   Seam ratification chain preceding this landing.
# - #53 instance commits `d908798`, `499ffd9`, `e910dd6` —
#   `grounded_claim` kind, citations are OIDs landed on main
#   prior to this shard's tick.
# - Task #272 — `forward_promise` kind (exempt from citation
#   check per the substrate's forward-promise honor).
# - Mara spec §3, projection-surface §6, doc-code-seam pre-review
#   — `grounded_claim` kind, citations are substrate document
#   paths whose ancestor commits exist on main.
# - The predicate substance framing itself — `motivating_claim`
#   kind (naming the "why" of the trio; no citation obligation).
# - TICK 4 forward-promise (`@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_ungrounded`)
#   — `forward_promise` kind (exempt).
# - The circular-reflexive verdict claim in this section is a
#   `candidate_claim` — the shard's own docblock cannot decide
#   its own grounding at analytical altitude; promotion to
#   `grounded_claim` awaits the extractor body + the sibling
#   fracture body + independent second-witness audit.
#
# Verdict: `both_survive` — the shard's docblock passes real
# survival (analytical citations resolve; forward-promises are
# honored) but phantom survival is also non-empty (the extractor
# body has not landed; `cited_content_matches_claim` cannot
# concretely check byte-match yet; the substrate can only decide
# this at the sub-Turing altitude when the extractor discharges).
# Promotion to `real_survives` awaits: extractor body (TICK 2
# forward-promise) + fracture body (TICK 4) + Seam second-witness
# audit at analytical altitude on the extracted predicate. Per
# Mara spec §Cross-cutting: this is the honest verdict at THIS
# shard's state.

---

in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/property
in @epistemologic/liquid_extraction
in @docblock

prism @epistemologic/property/docblock_grounded {
  focus docblock_grounded
  project docblock_grounded
  split docblock_grounded
  shift docblock_grounded
  settle docblock_grounded
}

# === docblock_grounded predicate (declarative half) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING PREDICATE. Returns verdict that every extractable
# claim in `d` is either an exempt kind (motivating_claim or
# forward_promise) or has a citation whose ancestor exists on main
# with cited-content matching the claim's text. Per Mara spec §3
# predicate substance:
#
#   docblock_grounded(d) ⇔
#     ∀ claim ∈ extract_claims(d):
#       claim.kind ∈ {motivating_claim, forward_promise} ∨
#       (claim.citation ≠ empty_ref ∧
#        ancestor_exists_on_main(claim.citation) ∧
#        cited_content_matches_claim(claim.citation, claim.text))
#
# Body discharges at splinter(ast) altitude via the liquid-extraction
# surface's `extract_predicate` output; the operational half at
# `@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_ungrounded` (TICK 4 forward-promise
# per Mara spec §4) emits a Tomm-circular question naming the missing
# ancestor when this predicate fails.
docblock_grounded(d: docblock) -> verdict { \ }

out @epistemologic/property/docblock_grounded
out docblock_grounded
